note as N1
  update() order (runs every egui frame)
  1. poll_export_job(): drain the worker channel, update ExportProgressModal, on Finished/Failed close it and (Failed) open ErrorModal.
  2. If screen is Editor: playback.tick(now) (may change the selected frame, then ctx.request_repaint_after(next_deadline)).
  3. Draw the current screen (WelcomeScreen::ui or EditorScreen::ui) -> Vec<AppAction> (blocked from input while a modal is open).
  4. Draw the modal (if any) centred, with a dimming layer over the screen. ModalOutcome::Accepted(action) / Cancelled closes it.
  5. for each AppAction collected in 3 and 4 -> handle_action(). Actions never run inside the draw code (no re-entrancy).
  on_close_requested(): if Editor and session.history.is_dirty() -> cancel the OS close, pending = QuitApplication,
  open ConfirmUnsavedModal; otherwise allow the close. If an export job is running: set its cancel flag, join the worker, then allow the close.
  Only ONE modal exists at a time. Opening a modal while one is open replaces it, EXCEPT ErrorModal which is shown
  after the current modal is closed (it replaces the current one only when the current one is NewProject/Save and the
  error came from its own action).
  Actions handled by the app because they need a service (see sequences 13b and 21a):
    OpenBrushEditor / SaveBrush / DeleteBrush -> Services.brushes (BrushStore persists brushes.json), then session.set_brush_library(copy).
    OpenImportModal -> FileDialogs.pick_file(["txt", "ascii"]) -> Services.importer.load(path) -> ImportModal.
    ApplyImport(req) -> session.import_content(req.file.to_buffer(req.ink), req.file.name, req.resize).
end note

note as N2
  - original / working: Rgba. UI: RGB sliders 0-255, an Alpha slider 0-255 (only when allow_alpha), hex field (#RRGGBB, or #RRGGBBAA when allow_alpha,
    validated live with Rgb::from_hex / Rgba::from_hex), 16 preset swatches, old/new preview drawn over a checkerboard so transparency is visible.
  - allow_alpha = true for InkColor and FillColor, false for FrameBackground (alpha is forced to 255 and the result is stored as Rgb).
  - "Apply to all frames" checkbox is only shown for ColorPickTarget::FrameBackground.
  - OK -> Accepted(ApplyColor(target, working, apply_to_all)).  Cancel / Esc -> Cancelled (nothing changes).
    InkColor -> session.set_ink_color, FillColor -> session.set_fill_color, FrameBackground -> session.set_frame_background(id, working.rgb(), all).
end note

note as N3
  Fields and validation (validate() runs when Create is pressed; the Create button is disabled while the form is invalid)
  - name: trimmed, 1..=64 chars, none of  / \ : * ? " < > |  and not ending with '.' or ' '. Default "Untitled".
  - folder: must exist and be writable. Default = <Documents>/AsciiPaint (created if missing). "Browse..." uses a native folder dialog.
  - target file = folder/name.aspr must NOT exist -> error "A project with this name already exists in this folder."
  - background: initial background colour of frame 1 (default #000000), edited with the same ColorPickerModal-style widget inline.
  - fps: 1..=60 (default 12).
  - canvas: shown read-only as "240 x 72 cells - 8 x 15 px" (the canvas can only grow later, through the import suggestion).
end note

note as N4
  - Format list grouped by scope:  Project: .aspr  |  Current frame: .png, .ascii  |  All frames: .aanim, ASCII image sequence (.ascii per frame), .mp4.
  - Everything except .aspr is a FLATTENED export: visible layers are composited, hidden layers are left out.
  - AnimationMp4 is disabled (greyed, tooltip "ffmpeg not found") when FfmpegLocator::find() returned None.
  - Default file name = project name (+ "_frame" + 3-digit 1-based index for FramePng / FrameAscii); extension follows the format.
    For AnimationAsciiSequence the file name field is the BASE name: the files are <base>_frame001.ascii ... <base>_frameNNN.ascii in the chosen folder
    (digits = max(3, digits of the frame count)). `sequence` is recomputed live and shown as "12 files: name_frame001.ascii ... name_frame012.ascii".
  - Save is enabled when folder exists, file_name is a valid file name (same rules as project name).
  - If the file already exists a confirmation line "File exists - it will be replaced" is shown (no extra dialog).
    For a sequence the line reads "3 of 12 files exist - they will be replaced" (sequence.existing).
end note

note as N5
  ImportModal (opened by AsciiPaintApp after the file was chosen and decoded, see diagram 21a and the state machine 11d)
  - Shows file name, kind (plain text / .ascii image), file size in cells (file.width x file.height) and the project canvas.
  - Plain text only: an ink colour swatch (default = current ink colour, opens the ColorPickerModal-style widget inline).
    .ascii files keep their own colours; their frame background colour is ignored.
  - fit = project_canvas.fit_content(file.width, file.height).
      Fits   -> one button [Import].
      TooBig -> the SUGGESTION panel: "The file is 300 x 90 cells, the project is 240 x 72."
                [Resize project to 300 x 90 and import]  [Import without resizing]  [Cancel]
                Without resizing it also says what is lost: "60 columns and 18 rows will be cut off."
                When the suggestion is capped at 1024 the panel adds what is still cut off after resizing.
  - request(true) -> ImportRequest{ resize: Some(suggested) },  request(false) -> ImportRequest{ resize: None }.
    [Import without resizing] is the "user refuses" path: the file is simply added as a layer, cut off at the page border.
end note

note as N6
  BrushEditorModal - the only place where characters are typed
  - Name field, Width / Height (1..=8), a grid of single-character text fields (empty field = None, the stamp cell does nothing),
    and an anchor picker (click a cell with the secondary button, or the Anchor radio row). A live preview paints the stamp with the current ink colour.
  - missing_glyphs: characters the font cannot draw (GlyphSource::contains == false) are listed with a warning; they are still allowed ('?' is drawn).
  - Save is enabled when to_brush() validates (see Brush::validate in diagram 04). Accepted(SaveBrush(brush)); editing = Some(id) keeps the id.
  - Built-in brushes open the editor as a copy (name "<name> copy"): they cannot be modified.
end note

