note as N1
  EditorSession is the single source of truth while a project is open. UI widgets mutate it ONLY through these methods.
  - add_frame()/duplicate_frame()/delete_frame()/move_frame(): build the matching Command (05), history.execute(), stop playback.
  - set_frame_background(id, c, all_frames): all_frames=false -> SetFrameBackgroundCommand (skipped when colour unchanged);
      all_frames=true -> CompositeCommand of one SetFrameBackgroundCommand per differing frame. history.execute().
  - set_fps() / set_looping(): SetPlaybackSettingsCommand. select_frame(i): timeline.select(i) (not undoable), keeps the selection mask.
  - Layers act on the SELECTED frame: select_layer(i) = frame.select_layer(i) (not undoable). add_layer() / duplicate_layer() / delete_layer() /
    move_layer() / set_layer_props() build AddLayerCommand / DeleteLayerCommand / MoveLayerCommand / SetLayerPropsCommand and history.execute().
  - undo()/redo(): see History rules; they stop playback first, apply UndoStep.selection with Selection::restore() when it is Some.
  - invert_selection(): selection.invert() (not undoable). delete_selection_contents(): when the selection is non-empty, clears BOTH planes of every
      selected cell of the active layer inside ONE PatchBuilder ("Clear selection"); needs a visible active layer.
  - copy(merged): needs a non-empty selection. merged = false -> CellBuffer::extract(active layer, selection); merged = true -> CellBuffer::extract_flat(
      Compositor::flatten(frame), selection). Stored with clipboard.set(). Not undoable, not dirty-making.
  - cut(): copy(false) then delete the selected cells through one PatchBuilder with label "Cut".
  - paste(): needs clipboard content. place_buffer_as_layer(buffer.clone(), "Pasted selection", None).
  - import_content(buf, name, resize): place_buffer_as_layer(buf, name, resize). Both share the same path:
      1. spec = resize.unwrap_or(project.canvas).  layer = buf.into_layer(frame.alloc_layer_id(), name, spec)  (cells outside the page are cut off).
      2. cmd = AddLayerCommand::with_layer(...); with resize: CompositeCommand("Import file") [ResizeCanvasCommand, cmd]; label "Paste layer" otherwise.
      3. before = selection.clone(); selection.resize(spec) when resized; selection.apply(buf.selected_cells((0, 0) offset, spec), Replace); after = selection.clone().
      4. history.execute_with_selection(cmd, project, SelectionChange{ before, after }).
      5. options.move_mode = Contents; set_tool(Move)  - the new layer is active and its cells are selected, so the user can drag it into place at once.
  - apply_picked(p): the only way the Pick tool changes anything: p.ink -> set_ink_color, p.fill -> set_fill_color. Not undoable, not dirty-making.
  - toggle_playback(): see state diagram 11 (playback). Starting playback cancels any busy tool.
  - set_brush_library(lib): replaces the brush list; if options.brush no longer exists it falls back to BrushLibrary::default_id().
end note

note as N2
  Geometry (page = canvas.pixel_width x canvas.pixel_height "page pixels", origin = screen position of the page top-left
  relative to the canvas widget's top-left)
  - page_px = (screen - view.min - origin) / zoom
  - cell    = (floor(page_px.x / cell_w), floor(page_px.y / cell_h)); None when outside 0..cols / 0..rows.
  - cell_rect(c) = [origin + (c.col*cell_w, c.row*cell_h)*zoom, size (cell_w, cell_h)*zoom] in widget coordinates.
  - zoom_at(cursor, notches): z' = clamp(zoom * WHEEL_STEP^notches, MIN_ZOOM, MAX_ZOOM);
      origin' = (cursor - view.min) - ((cursor - view.min) - origin) * (z' / zoom); zoom = z'.   (point under cursor stays fixed)
  - pan_by(d): origin += d, then clamp so that at least 64 screen px of the page stay visible on each axis.
  - fit(): zoom = clamp(min(view.w / page_w, view.h / page_h) * 0.95, MIN, MAX); page centred in the view.
  - actual_size(): zoom = 1.0 (1 page pixel = 1 screen pixel); page centred.
  - zoom_step(+1/-1): z' = clamp(zoom * 1.25^dir) around the view centre. A new Editor opens with fit().
  - After an import resized the canvas the viewport keeps zoom and origin (the page just gets bigger to the right / bottom).
end note

note as N3
  Input mapping (translate_input)
  - Mouse wheel over the canvas = zoom_at(cursor, scroll_y / 50.0). (Never scrolls.)
  - Middle-button drag, or Space held + left drag = pan_by(drag delta). Space-pan suppresses tool events.
  - Primary button and plain pointer movement -> ToolEvent::PointerDown / PointerMove / PointerUp / DoubleClick with cell = screen_to_cell(...).
    PointerMove is also sent while no button is pressed (hover previews).
  - Enter/Backspace/Delete/Arrows/Escape -> ToolEvent::Key, only when the canvas has keyboard focus (clicking the canvas gives focus; text fields
    elsewhere take it away). There is NO character typing on the canvas: printable keys are not translated.
  - Returns the hovered cell for the StatusBar.
  - When dispatch() answers ToolResponse::Picked(colours), CanvasView calls session.apply_picked(colours) (ink -> set_ink_color, fill -> set_fill_color).
  - Painting order: see CanvasRenderer note.
end note

note as N4
  paint() draw order (only the cells returned by Viewport::visible_cells are visited)
  0. flat = cached Compositor::flatten(selected frame), recomputed only when (frame id, Frame.revision) changed. Hidden layers are not part of it.
  1. Dark neutral workspace fill (#2B2B2B) over the whole widget.
  2. PAGE: filled rect with timeline.selected_frame().background.
  3. For each visible cell with flat.fill.a > 0: fill the cell rect with flat.fill (straight alpha, drawn over the page colour).
  4. For each visible cell with glyph != ' ': textured quad from GlyphAtlas::uv(glyph), tinted with flat.ink (straight alpha -> premultiplied for egui).
  5. Grid lines (1 px, white at 12% opacity) when show_grid && zoom >= 2.0.
  6. Selection: boundary_edges() (cached by Selection::revision) as 1.5 px dashed black/white "marching ants".
  7. Tool overlay: brush footprint outline (Paint / Erase hover), rect/ellipse preview, polygon rubber-band, hovered-cell outline, and for the Move tool the
     floating cells drawn on top of everything at their offset plus the shifted selection outline.
  8. Page border (1 px #000000 at 60%).
  While Playing, steps 6-7 are skipped. The glyph cache key is only the char, the colour is applied by the vertex tint.
  The active layer is not highlighted on the canvas; the canvas always shows the composited result.
end note

note as N5
  tick(now, tl) -> Option<Duration> = time until the next frame change (for ctx.request_repaint_after) or None when Stopped.
  See the Playback state machine (11) for the exact transitions.
end note

note as N6
  Layout (top to bottom): header "Frames" | scrollable list of FrameItem | [+ Add] [Duplicate] [Delete] |
  separator | "Background" swatch + hex text of the SELECTED frame | FPS field | [Play/Pause] [x] Loop.
  - FrameItem = 1-based index label + thumbnail (ThumbnailCache, composited result) + highlight when selected. Click = select_frame(i).
  - Drag a FrameItem: FrameDrag{from, hover_slot}; on release, if hover_slot != from -> move_frame(from, to).
  - Delete is disabled when timeline.len() == 1. Add inserts AFTER the selected frame and selects it.
  - Background swatch click -> AppAction::OpenColorPicker(ColorPickTarget::FrameBackground(selected frame id)).
    The hex field commits on Enter / focus loss (valid #RRGGBB only, otherwise reverts) via set_frame_background(id, c, false).
  - FPS = DragValue 1..=60 integer, commits via set_fps() (Enter / focus loss / drag release). Loop checkbox -> set_looping().
  - All edit buttons are disabled while Playing, except Play/Pause itself and frame selection (which stops playback).
end note

note as N7
  ToolOptionsBar = the top bar under the menu. It shows the sections of the ACTIVE tool and edits session.options only through the session setters.
  sections_for(tool):
    Paint  : BrushPicker, PlaneToggles, InkColor, FillColor
    Fill   : BrushPicker, PlaneToggles, InkColor, FillColor            (the picked brush supplies the fill character)
    Pick   : PlaneToggles, PickSourceButtons, Hint("Click a cell. Foreground picks its character colour, Background picks its background colour.")
    Erase  : EraseSize, PlaneToggles
    SelectRect / SelectPolygon / SelectEllipse : SelectionModeButtons, SelectionActions
    Move   : MoveModeButtons, SelectionActions, Hint("Drag inside the selection. Arrow keys nudge, Shift = 10 cells.")
  - BrushPicker: drop-down listing the brushes with a small stamp preview, then [New...] [Edit...] [Delete]
    (-> OpenBrushEditor(None) / OpenBrushEditor(Some(id)) / DeleteBrush(id); Edit and Delete are disabled for built-in brushes except that Edit opens a copy).
  - PlaneToggles: two toggle buttons [Foreground] [Background]; both may be on. They decide which plane(s) Paint, Fill and Erase write.
  - InkColor / FillColor: swatches (drawn over a checkerboard, alpha visible) -> OpenColorPicker(InkColor / FillColor).
  - EraseSize: DragValue 1..=16.
  - SelectionModeButtons: [Replace] [Add] [Subtract] (a held Shift / Alt overrides the button).  SelectionActions: [All] [None] [Invert] (Invert disabled with no selection).
  - MoveModeButtons: [Contents] [Outline only].  PickSourceButtons: [Merged] [Active layer].
  - The PlaneToggles of the Pick tool are the same toggles as Paint's: they choose which colour is picked (Foreground -> ink colour, Background -> fill colour).
  - Everything is disabled while Playing.
end note

note as N8
  LayerPanel (right side, under the Frames panel). Lists the layers of the SELECTED frame TOP FIRST (row 0 = layers[len - 1]).
  - LayerRow = eye checkbox (visible) + name label (double-click to rename: LayerPanel.renaming, commit on Enter / focus loss) + highlight when active.
    Click a row = select_layer(index). Eye click = set_layer_props(visible toggled).
  - Under the list, for the ACTIVE layer: Opacity slider 0-100 % (commits on release through set_layer_props).
  - Buttons: [+ Add] [Duplicate] [Delete]. Add and Duplicate are disabled at 64 layers, Delete when the frame has one layer.
  - Drag a LayerRow: LayerDrag{from, hover_slot} (row positions). On release the panel converts rows to layer indices (index = len - 1 - row)
    and calls move_layer(from, to) when the position changed.
  - A hidden active layer shows a small "hidden" badge; tools refuse to write into it.
  - All buttons and edits are disabled while Playing.
end note

note as N9
  Menus (MenuBar)
  File   : Open recent... | Save (Ctrl+S) | Save as / Export... | Import file... | Close project
  Edit   : Undo (Ctrl+Z) | Redo (Ctrl+Y) | Cut (Ctrl+X) | Copy (Ctrl+C) | Copy merged (Ctrl+Shift+C) | Paste (Ctrl+V) | Clear selection contents (Delete)
  Select : All (Ctrl+A) | None (Ctrl+D) | Invert (Ctrl+Shift+I)
  View   : Zoom in (Ctrl+=) | Zoom out (Ctrl+-) | Fit to window (Ctrl+0) | Actual size (Ctrl+1) | Show cell grid
  Cut / Copy / Copy merged / Clear need a non-empty selection, Paste needs clipboard content. The shortcuts are handled by
  EditorScreen::handle_shortcuts, never by a tool.
end note

